   "description": "Should founders leave home to build? In this compilation, Jeremy Au, Shiyan Koh, Adriel Yong and Chalinda Abeykoon argue that the better question is how often to go, and what to bring back. Shiyan, Managing Partner at Hustle Fund, tells founders outside the Bay Area to spend time in San Francisco every quarter or so, without necessarily moving there. Adriel, co-founder and COO of Clouted, argues that Singapore works so well it dulls the problem-solving instinct founders need, and that every student should spend six months to a year abroad. Chalinda, Managing Partner at nVentures, grew up in Colombo during Sri Lanka’s civil war, when leaving was the plan for almost everyone, and now runs a fund that backs Sri Lankan founders. They discuss why copying another ecosystem’s playbook has limits,"
